#X text 240 83 Supports variable speed playing \, pausing \, seeking
\, time-stretching and resampling;
#X text 240 123 The object reads a sound file from disk and plays it
through its audio outlets. You can control the playback position with
messages such as [seek] \, [rewind] and [ff] \, change the speed with
the @speed property \, enable looping with @loop and switch to time-stretching
mode with @stretch. The object also reports errors to a global receiver
name set via @on_err.;
